; --average-lot-prices cannot average the lots of one commodity whose
; prices are in different commodities, fixated or not: it fails with
; "Adding amounts with different commodities", naming the first two price
; commodities in the order `bal --lots` lists the lots, on every run.
; Assets:Two holds ETF bought at =EUR10 and at =$11, listed {=$11} first,
; so the error names '$' and then 'EUR'.  Assets:Three holds ETF bought
; at the floating prices EUR10, $11 and GBP9, and the error names '$' and
; 'EUR' again.
;
; Ledger used to name the first two price commodities it met in the order
; in which the balance happened to keep its lots, which could change from
; one run to the next: for Assets:Three, 3.4.1 named 'EUR' and '$' on most
; runs and 'EUR' and 'GBP' on the others.

2024/01/01 Buy in euros
    Assets:Two       2 ETF @ =EUR10
    Assets:Cash

2024/02/01 Buy in dollars
    Assets:Two       2 ETF @ =$11
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/02 Buy in euros
    Assets:Three     2 ETF @ EUR10
    Assets:Cash

2024/02/02 Buy in dollars
    Assets:Three     2 ETF @ $11
    Assets:Cash

2024/03/02 Buy in pounds
    Assets:Three     2 ETF @ GBP9
    Assets:Cash

test bal --average-lot-prices Assets:Two -> 1
__ERROR__
While calling function 'averaged_lots 2 ETF {=$11} [2024/02/01]
2 ETF {=EUR10} [2024/01/01]':
Error: Adding amounts with different commodities: '$' != 'EUR'
end test

test bal --average-lot-prices Assets:Three -> 1
__ERROR__
While calling function 'averaged_lots 2 ETF {$11} [2024/02/02]
2 ETF {EUR10} [2024/01/02]
2 ETF {GBP9} [2024/03/02]':
Error: Adding amounts with different commodities: '$' != 'EUR'
end test
